From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:41:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: icc-rpm: backport the 7.4 vote fixes

Four commits of v7.4-rc1, in upstream order:

 51797517fab7 interconnect: qcom: Move bcm_div() to common code
 40ea86fa389c interconnect: qcom: icc-rpm: Don't skip small votes
 b2079a6b8e8b interconnect: qcom: icc-rpm: Handle icc_link_create() failures
 24e7422ce311 interconnect: qcom: use 64-bit SMD RPM bus votes

The first three are 1-3 of "icc_rpm_smd_qol"
<20260909-topic-icc_rpm_smd_qol-v1-1-6dc5b5e97626@oss.qualcomm.com>; the
first only gives icc-rpm the rounding helper the second uses. The fourth
is <20260904-topic-icc_rpm_64b_req-v1-1-37e24f1991a3@oss.qualcomm.com>.

The fourth matters most here: SMD RPM bus votes carry a 64-bit value, but
the driver sent a u32 and told the RPM the payload was 4 bytes. The SM6115's
DDR slave (EBI) vote sums every master, and the MANGMI Air X's CPU OPPs alone
ask for up to 8.37 GB/s, so its vote wrapped past 4 GiB/s.

Not taken: ddbacca26d1d (auxiliary QoS ports) and its two users, which are
MSM8996 and MSM8976 nodes; SM6115 and QCM2290 nodes have none.

Applies after our 0132 (both edit icc-rpm.c).

Signed-off-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
